baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa67ea6e6-2a2c-41aa-b480-8dcbb42b7afc_1024x576.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>Mentalization is a powerful modality. I used to run a practice on Grand Street in Brooklyn, NY.  We created our own “Grand Rounds”, and in this episode, I presented an hour-long version of “My MBT Talk,” where I give an overview of Mentalization-Based Treatment.  The book on the topic I co-edited with <a href=\"https://amzn.to/3tv2sGh\">Laurel Williams, D.O., is available here.</a></p><p>I don’t work at Brooklyn Minds anymore.  <a href=\"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/curated-mental-health-partners-with-brooklyn-minds-psychiatry-to-scale-breakthrough-treatments-for-mental-illness-301527846.html\">Others acquired that practice.</a> Carlene and I have had no role in that entity.</p><p>We now run a practice called <a href=\"https://www.fermata.health\">Fermata</a>.  It’s in North Brooklyn and focuses on accelerated neuromodulation treatment.  <a href=\"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/irxreminder-announces-enrollment-of-initial-patients-in-groundbreaking-tardive-dyskinesia-detection-study-301891941.html\">We also run clinical trials…</a></p><p><a href=\"http://info@fermata.health\">info@fermata.health</a> is the email for inquiries.</p><p>I just returned from teaching at the <a href=\"https://www.menningerclinic.org/treatment/treatment-for-adults\">Menninger Clinic</a> on MBT, and continue to provide ongoing supervision for therapists as an <a href=\"https://www.annafreud.org\">Anna Freud Centre</a> Supervisor.  Carlene and I will also be presenting with friends and co-authors at the <a href=\"https://www.aacap.org\">AACAP</a> Conference in 2 weeks here in NYC!</p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p>","text":"Mentalization is a powerful modality. I used to run a practice on Grand Street in Brooklyn, NY. We created our own “Grand Rounds”, and in this episode, I presented an hour-long version of “My MBT Talk,” where I give an overview of Mentalization-Based Treatment. The book on the topic I co-edited with Laurel Williams, D.O., is available here.\n\nI don’t work at Brooklyn Minds anymore. Others acquired that practice. Carlene and I have had no role in that entity.\n\nWe now run a practice called Fermata . It’s in North Brooklyn and focuses on accelerated neuromodulation treatment. We also run clinical trials…\n\ninfo@fermata.health is the email for inquiries.\n\nI just returned from teaching at the Menninger Clinic on MBT, and continue to provide ongoing supervision for therapists as an Anna Freud Centre Supervisor. Carlene and I will also be presenting with friends and co-authors at the AACAP Conference in 2 weeks here in NYC!\n\nSubscribe now"}